 {
  "name": "Anderson, John H.",
  "note": "John H. Anderson taught at the I. C. Y. in the early eighties. He was educated in New York State, and after a short tenure here, went West, and continued his profession. Malachi Dunmore Cornish was born April 11, 1860 in Philadelphia, Pa. He is the son of David and Rachel Cornish. He attended the James Forten Grammar School (formerly the Bird School) and the Institute for Colored Youth, 9th and Bainbridge Sts., Philadelphia, Pa., graduating from the latter school in June, 1878."
 },
