 {
  "name": "Armstead, William H. F.",
  "note": "William H. F. Armstead was for many years head of the Camden, N. J., grammar school, and was later on succeeded by Malachi Cornish, who still holds the position. Among the former pupils of the I. C. Y. to graduate from the U. of P. are: James T. Potter, George R. Hilton, Eugene T. Hinson, William H. Warrick, Conwell Banton, Hiram Williams. William E. Augusta, Andrew F. Hill and John H. Smythe were three I. C. Y. graduates to serve as cashiers of banks under the Freedmen's Bureau."
 },
