 {
  "name": "Barney, Laura F.",
  "note": "Laura F. Barney, was born in Philadelphia. Her first schooling was in the Friends' School, Byberry, 23d ward. She entered the I. C. Y. and graduated in 1871. She taught at Chester, Pa., and then in Washington, D. C., finally becoming Assistant Superintendent of the High School there, where she had the finest rating. In the list of the premier teachers in the Washington, D. C., schools the following were from the I. C. Y.: Laura F. and Maria C. Barney, Sarah L."
 },
