  "note": ""
 },
 {
  "name": "Bassett, Charlotte",
  "note": "Charlotte Bassett. --Miss Bassett was the daughter of the Hon. E. D. Bassett. She was a graduate of the Institute and began her career there as a teacher soon after graduation. Upon the closing of the Institute, in 1902, she was appointed an assistant in the Octavius V. Catto School. With the passing of the Catto School, she was transferred to the Durham School. Here her efficient work led to her appointment as teacher in the grammar department."
 },
