 {
  "name": "Catto, Octavius V.",
  "note": "Octavius V. Catto was born in Charleston, S. C., February 22, 1840, but came to Philadelphia with his parents at an early age. He attended the Institute for Colored Youth and graduated therefrom as the valedictorian of his class in 1858. He was immediately appointed assistant to the Principal, the late Hon. E. D. Bassett, as teacher of English and Mathematics."
 },
