 {
  "name": "Dorsey, Charles A.",
  "note": "Charles A. Dorsey, a native of Philadelphia; his first school life was at Birds School, now the James Forten, then at the I. C. Y., under Prof. Chas. L. Reason. He left and matriculated at Oberlin College, Ohio, graduating therefrom in 1863. He immediately accepted the Principalship of a large school in Brooklyn, and taught for more than forty-five years. He was before his career closed, school supervisor of Brooklyn."
 },
