 {
  "name": "McKane, Alice Woodby",
  "note": "Alice Woodby McKane, now a practicing physician in Boston, is one among many graduates of the I. C. Y. who has had an active and interesting career. With her husband, she established a hospital at Savannah, Ga., and at Monrovia, west coast of Africa. Edward Alexander Bouchet, born September 15th, 1852, at New Haven, Conn., prepared for college in New Haven High School and Hopkins Grammar School, New Haven. Entered Yale College, 1870. Graduated, A. B., 1874, and received the degree Ph."
